{
  "id": "Compound::DB00917 - Gene::5734",
  "verbalization": "Dinoprostone, a prostaglandin analogue, is linked to Ptger4 through a series of molecular interactions that involve prostaglandin receptors. The evidence suggests that Dinoprostone binds to Ptger2, which then participates in prostaglandin receptor activity. This activity is further associated with Ptger4, indicating a potential functional relationship between Dinoprostone and the receptor. The presence of anaphylactoid syndrome of pregnancy, caused by Misoprostol, which binds to Ptger4, adds another layer of complexity, suggesting that Dinoprostone may influence the same receptor pathway through its binding to Ptger2. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Dinoprostone could modulate Ptger4 activity, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
